                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: Both constructors call fs::create_directories(configPersistPath) before appending \"/config\" and calling serialize().\nThe parent directory is guaranteed to exist by the time serialize() runs. \nConsider removing this block."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-ldap-config/ldap_config.cpp",
                    "line": 748,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-ldap-config/ldap_config.cpp",
                    "line": 766,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "Please either keep the throwing overload or add elog<InternalFailure>() when ec is set."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-ldap-config/ldap_config.cpp",
                    "line": 766,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
                        "email": "raviteja28031990@gmail.com",
                        "username": "raviteja-b"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-ldap-config/ldap_config.cpp",
                    "line": 776,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "cereal writes through it via os.write() into the stream's userspace buffer.\nWithout os.flush() before the os.good() check, only buffer-level errors are caught, not disk write failures. \nConsider adding os.flush() before the check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-ldap-config/ldap_config.cpp",
                    "line": 776,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ravi Teja",
